      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<br>In the Kaplan turbine water is entered into the spiral casing of the
    turbine which maintains the pressure flow after that it moves to the guide vanes.
    From guide vanes, the water turns through 90\xB0 and flows axially through the
    runner blade connected to the generator's shaft to produce electricity. Let us
    understand how it works in detail."
